{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Run the Node.js application on node1 in a rootless Podman container using nodeapp, with both container and service named node-hello.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Final observations show node-hello.service running as nodeapp (UID 1000), Podman reporting rootless=true with nodeapp-owned storage, a running container named node-hello, and the Node.js process executing /app/server.js inside it.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a1c28a27122a4cae","cmd-b6949d395c9a46b4","cmd-e82f935693784f5b","cmd-640f4b9abaec4082"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Return exactly `Hello, world!` from `/` on TCP port 8080.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The final probe directly observed a 0.0.0.0:8080 listener, HTTP 200 from `/`, and a 13-byte body whose exact and hexadecimal comparisons equal `Hello, world!`.","evidence_ids":["cmd-23a6318160b64a16","cmd-640f4b9abaec4082","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Start the application without requiring an interactive login.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The service is enabled, nodeapp has a nologin shell and lingering enabled, and a bounded stop/start transition showed the service, container, and listener disappear before systemd restored the endpoint with the exact response while nodeapp remained non-login.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a1c28a27122a4cae","cmd-23a6318160b64a16","cmd-4092f05747194ec8","cmd-4497691c13314753","cmd-640f4b9abaec4082"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.96,"summary":"Final lifecycle checks show no failed services and healthy package-manager state. The required port 8080 listener is the only meaningful new exposure. Four small executor-created HTTP probe files remain in /tmp, constituting minor residue.","evidence_ids":["global:before_prepare:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},"overall_summary":"All material outcomes are satisfied with direct final-state and transition evidence: the correctly named Node.js container runs rootlessly as nodeapp, serves the exact required response on port 8080, and can be started through enabled systemd service control without an interactive login.","limitations":["No full host reboot was captured; unattended startup is demonstrated through an enabled system service and a controlled stop/start transition rather than a boot-cycle test."]}
